-dev%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","type":"Bot","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lovable-dev%5Bbot%5D","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Victups/Projeto-Final-EngSoft-II/commits/697df960fc88fbbdf74daea11c9993e3e4e8f184/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2025-09-02T11:34:51Z","email":"159125892+gpt-engineer-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"gpt-engineer-app[bot]"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2025-09-02T11:34:51Z","email":"159125892+gpt-engineer-app[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","name":"gpt-engineer-app[bot]"},"message":"Fix SonarCloud issues and migrate to Jest\n\nThis commit addresses various issues reported by SonarCloud, including:\n- Avoiding array index in keys for lists.\n- Removing useless variable assignments.\n- Extracting nested ternary operations.\n- Removing unused imports.\n- Moving component definitions out of parent components.\n- Using optional chaining for conciseness.\n- Associating form labels with controls.\n- Fixing conditional React Hook calls.\n- Refactoring functions to reduce cognitive complexity.\n- Avoiding non-native interactive elements and ensuring keyboard accessibility.\n- Using concise character class syntax for regex.\n- Improving accessibility with appropriate HTML elements and roles.\n- Wrapping Context provider values in useMemo.\n- Completing TODO comments.\n- Refactoring nested functions.\n- Marking never-reassigned members as readonly.\n- Using RegExp.exec() instead of exec().\n- Correcting unnecessary escape characters in regex.\n- Defining constants for duplicated literals in SQL migrations.\n- Adding explicit ASC for order clauses in SQL migrations.\n\nAdditionally, this commit includes the migration from Vite testing to Jest and sets up the necessary configurations for test coverage calculation.","tree":{"sha":"ea9f72f27d27752aa9467725bcaeaddde0c6d74e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Victups/Projeto-Final-EngSoft-II/git/trees/ea9f72f27d27752aa9467725bcaeaddde0c6